    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Solo Travelers Rainy-Day Planning</h1>
    <p>Rain in Hanoi arrives on its own schedule and a solo rider meets it alone. There is no passenger to hold the map dry, no companion to share the decision to stop, and no one to laugh with under a cafe awning while the street turns into a river. Rainy-day planning is therefore a solo skill of its own: reading the day honestly, gearing up properly, riding within wet-condition margins, and knowing exactly when not to ride. This guide covers all of it.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for the solo-traveler profile. Verified rental prices for the whole fleet are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general rental questions are on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the bike that fits a flexible, plan-shifting trip is chosen in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/solo-travelers-bike-choice/">solo travelers bike choice</a> guide.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">What rain means for a solo rider</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Reading the day honestly</a></li>
